<% content_for :title, "stylish — salon appointment booking (Kiosk demo)" %>

  <div class="agentbar">
    <span class="tag">🤖 For agents</span>
    <span>Agents &amp; AI assistants — <a href="/.well-known/kiosk.json">learn here</a> how to work with this site.</span>
    <a class="what" href="https://kiosk.tech">(what is this?)</a>
  </div>
  <header>
    <div class="logo">styl<span>ish</span></div>
    <nav class="tagline">salon booking · Combette on Park</nav>
  </header>

  <div class="wrap">

    <!-- ── 1. Two entrances — visitor or staff ───────────────────────── -->
    <section class="sec">
      <div class="sec-k">🤖 Try it with your own assistant</div>
      <div class="tryit">
        <h2>An AI assistant books here for you</h2>
        <p>stylish is a salon your AI assistant books with directly. There are <strong>two entrances</strong>. Pick <strong>one</strong>: come in as a <strong>visitor</strong> <em>or</em> as <strong>staff</strong>. One assistant cannot be both at once.</p>

        <div class="linkbox">
          <strong>① Visitor entrance — book any service.</strong>
          Tell your AI assistant:
          <p class="say">“Book a haircut at stylish.demo.kiosk.tech.”</p>
          It finds the salon, signs itself up, reads the <strong>service menu</strong>, picks a service and books. You need no account and no app. <strong>The salon always has room:</strong> every service is open at any time, for any number of bookings. Your booking is real: it goes into the salon's book and the staff see it.
        </div>

        <div class="linkbox">
          <strong>② Staff entrance — see the whole book.</strong>
          Use <a href="/users/sign_in"><strong>Staff login</strong></a> to sign in as the salon owner. Open <a href="/kiosk/auth/assistants">Manage&nbsp;assistants</a> and press <strong>Get a link code</strong>. Give the code to your assistant: it now acts <strong>as the owner</strong>, because the salon's staff list says you are the owner. Ask it for <code>salon_calendar</code>. <strong>The owner's assistant sees every booking with its price</strong>, so it can tell you the € revenue the book will bring in. A visitor's assistant sees only its own bookings.
          <div class="cred">Demo staff login (owner): <code>owner@stylish.example</code> &nbsp;/&nbsp; <code>stylish-demo-password</code></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── 2. About this demo ────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="sec">
      <div class="sec-k">About this demo</div>
      <div class="about">
        <p><strong>stylish</strong> (the salon: Combette on Park) is a salon-booking demo. It has a small menu of services, each with a price in euros. Every service can always be booked, as many times as people like, so the salon never fills up. It shows how a salon's staff list decides what an assistant may see. A staff member links their assistant to their own account, and the assistant gets their job. With <code>salon_calendar</code>, the owner's assistant sees every booking and its price. A visitor's assistant sees only its own bookings.</p>
        <div class="chips">
          <span class="chip">✂️ Small service menu</span>
          <span class="chip">♾️ Always bookable</span>
          <span class="chip">🪪 Staff jobs decide what the assistant sees</span>
          <span class="chip">💶 Forecasted € revenue</span>
          <span class="chip">Link your account to your assistant</span>
        </div>
        <div class="links">
          <a href="https://github.com/kiosk-hq/kiosk/tree/main/kiosk-demo-stylish">▶ Source on GitHub</a>
          <a href="https://kiosk.tech">What is Kiosk? →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── 3. Live activity (compact) ────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="sec">
      <div class="sec-k">Live activity</div>
      <div class="stats">
        <div class="stat"><div class="n"><%= @services %></div><div class="l">Services on the menu</div></div>
        <div class="stat"><div class="n">∞</div><div class="l">Capacity (always open)</div></div>
        <div class="stat"><div class="n"><%= @appointments_booked %></div><div class="l">Booked so far</div></div>
        <div class="stat"><div class="n"><%= @forecast_eur %></div><div class="l">Forecasted revenue</div></div>
      </div>
    </section>

  </div>

  <!-- ── 4. The storefront — what a human visitor sees (separated) ────── -->
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="store">
      <div class="store-label">The storefront — what a human visitor sees</div>
      <div class="store-body">
        <div class="hero">
          <h1>Book my next haircut.</h1>
          <p>Combette on Park — cuts, colour and styling, booked in a single conversation.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
